<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Checks Angle's radians <-> HMS conversions and ShortestDistance over HOUR ANGLES.

    A standalone console exe, matching the other Test* projects here, rather than an MSTest
    class: it can be built and run without a test runner, and AngleTestProject - the one place
    that does have a test framework - no longer compiles (42 references to Angle.Type, which is
    now Angle.AngleType) and is not in the solution.

    net48/x86 to match Common.

    Deliberately a plain Reference with a HintPath rather than a ProjectReference: a
    ProjectReference rebuilds Common into bin\Debug, i.e. the AnyCPU path, and "AnyCPU newer
    than x86" is the signal used to catch a build that forgot /p:Platform=x86.  Building this
    test should not disturb that.  Build Common first if this cannot find it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
    <PlatformTarget>x86</PlatformTarget>
    <AssemblyName>TestAngleHa</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>TestAngleHa</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Reference Include="Common">
      <HintPath>..\Common\bin\x86\Debug\Common.dll</HintPath>
      <Private>true</Private>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
